<% character = roll.player.character %><% used = character.items.used_since(roll.scene.created_at) %>In scene <%= roll.scene.position %> of <%= roll.scene.game_session.scene_budget %>, <%= roll.scene.part_of_the_story %>, <%= roll.player.name %> chose "<%= roll.choice.label %>": die <%= roll.value %>, modifier <%= format("%+d", roll.modifier) %>, statuses <%= format("%+d", roll.status_modifier) %>, total <%= roll.total %> against <%= roll.target %>. <%= roll.grade_label %>, margin <%= format("%+d", roll.margin) %>.<% if roll.grade == :narrow %> It works, but not for free: it costs <%= roll.player.name %> something on the way.<% elsif !roll.success? %> It does not work, and that costs something within the plan: time, someone's trust, a clue or health. The story takes no new direction from it and offers no second try at the same thing.<% end %>
<% if used.any? %>Used since the scene began, already applied: <%= used.map { |item| "#{item.name} (#{format("%+d", item.hp_effect)} health)" }.join(", ") %>.
<% end %><%= roll.player.name %> now: <%= character.sheet %>.
<% if (companions = roll.scene.companions).any? %>In the scene with <%= roll.player.name %>: <%= companions.map { it.character.portrait }.join("; ") %>.
<% end %><% game = roll.scene.game_session %><% if roll.scene.last? %><% verdict = game.verdict %><% earlier = game.rolls.where.not(id: roll) %>This is the last roll, and the story ends with it, in <%= verdict %>: <%= earlier.where(success: true).count %> of the <%= earlier.count %> rolls before it succeeded. Tell what this roll does, then how the story ends. The ending is only what the choices and rolls bring about: no one, <%= game.party.map(&:name).to_sentence %> included, makes a move in it that those did not set up.<% if game.party.many? %> Each of them has a part in it: <%= game.party.reject(&:departed?).map { |player| "#{player.name} tried #{player.attempts.to_sentence.presence || "nothing"}" }.join("; ") %>.<% end %> The block adds "outcome": "<%= verdict %>".
<% elsif roll.life_at_stake? %>This roll can take the last of <%= roll.player.name %>'s health. If it does, <%= roll.player.name %> falls and the story ends here in defeat: tell how, and add "outcome": "defeat" to the block. If not, tell only what this roll does, in a paragraph or two, and stop there: the next scene comes in my next message.
<% else %>Tell only what this roll does, in a paragraph or two, and stop there: the next scene comes in my next message.
<% end %>